{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4719",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is implicated in the regulation of Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) Activity through its interaction with Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, which are subunits of the complex that participates in the activity of Ndufs1. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to these subunits, thereby influencing the overall function of the complex that ultimately interacts with Ndufs1. This mechanism implies that Metformin may modulate the activity of Ndufs1 through a pathway involving the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust relationship, highlighting the role of Ndufa12 and Ndufv3 in mediating this interaction. The integration of these findings suggests that Metformin's effect on Ndufs1 is likely mediated through a regulatory mechanism involving the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex, which is a key component of mitochondrial respiration.",
